  "notable_features": "Commonly glorified as 'Sarva Gamaka Māṇika Rakti Rāgaṃ'. It is the 5th raga in the 5th chakra Bāṇa; mnemonic name Bāṇa-Ma. It has many janya ragas and is among the melakarta ragas with the highest number of derivatives. Its swaras are evenly spaced, giving strong melodic appeal and wide scope for elaboration, experimentation, and phrase exploration. Through graha bhedam it yields Kalyani, Hanumatodi, Natabhairavi, Kharaharapriya, and Harikambhoji. The 7th graha-bhedam result has both madhyamams and no panchamam, so it is not accepted as a valid melakarta. In simplified form, it corresponds to the white keys of a piano/keyboard. It is the shuddha madhyamam counterpart of Kalyani. Sami Ninne is noted as usually the first varnam taught to Carnatic music students. It is also one of the major concert ragas with large scope for improvisation and expansive manodharma."
